  "review": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "W-CONFIGURATION-CHAT, W-EFFECTIVE-SETTINGS and W-CONFIGURATION-PROPOSAL consume private native snapshots and refuse credential edits. Encoded credentials and unreadable parameter components stay private, while safe URLs, identifiers and explicit separate confirmation remain usable. NATIVE-CONFIG-URL-PARAMETERS maps the new distinguishing assertions to these existing widgets.",
    "implementation": "Reviewed nativeSnapshot/nativeRedactor, exported and agent-tool inspection, propose/confirm/apply and startup sanitation. Private fields, token patterns, arbitrary header values and known copied values are hidden without changing raw native startup input. BeforeDigest retains raw freshness for confirmation and deferred application. URL parsing uses RawQuery and EscapedFragment; incomplete parameter parses remove that component, and raw/decoded values are collected without decoding fragment separators first. Fragment reconstruction preserves its valid escaped form. Safe named identifiers, selectors and ordinary settings remain usable. Startup sanitizes entities before projections and journal copies in one paged transaction; event identity/state is preserved without replay. Existing cached/background API ownership, cancellation and admission are unchanged. Original encoded userinfo is collected from the parsed URL authority alongside decoded username/password values, preserving copied noncanonical percent escapes that User.String would normalize.",
    "tests": "Read all eight native regression functions and their actual assertions. Inspection tests cover both exported and agent-tool views, exact selectors, MaxInt64 and copied URL/header values. Named-entry tests distinguish safe names/edits from nested credential fields. Freshness tests make hidden rotation invalidate confirmation, then apply one exact fresh edit. Rejection tests require no saved proposal or native write. Legacy migration crosses 32-row pages with 37 matching events, proves rollback after one rewrite, preserves metadata/state and is idempotent. New TestNativeURLParameterBoundariesRejectCredentials has eight isolated cases covering semicolons, invalid escapes, encoded delimiters, escaped username/password userinfo and raw/decoded copies across inspection, saved proposals, legacy entities/events and refusal before persistence. These cases and the strengthened shared migration fixture failed before the URL correction. The public-URL regression now applies three safe URLs independently, including semicolon anchors and escaped noncredential fragments, with exact spelling and one write per case only after confirmation. Focused regressions and factory race checks pass; required reconciliation is run separately. Fixture success establishes no installed-host acceptance. Encoded-userinfo cases independently failed before the raw-authority collection was added; assertions compare JSON-escaped raw and decoded copies so a noncanonical percent escape cannot evade the check."
  },
